In organizations, there are many ways to communicate and train. Some of the more common ways are:
1. Written communications, such as letters and emails;
2. Phone calls, text messages, and instant messages;
3. Meeting face-to-face, such as brainstorming, training, and brainstorming sessions;
4. Together-meeting in person, such as a team meeting, or a company retreat;
5. Video conferencing, such as conference calls, or meetings over the internet;
6. In-person activities, such as team building, scrum meetings, or meeting in person
